  "id": "nhac_tre_saigon",
  "name": "Nhạc trẻ (1960s-70s Saigon rock and soul)",
  "family": "rock",
  "lineage": "Youth music of Saigon in roughly 1966-1975, played by local bands and singers in clubs, at dance parties and on radio for young Vietnamese audiences and American servicemen, mixing covers of Anglo-American rock, soul and go-go hits with Vietnamese-language songs in the same styles. The recordings were rediscovered through reissue compilations from 2010 onward.",
  "recipe": "classic Asian nhạc trẻ, distorted Rock, regional branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment. single coil electric guitar, electric bass, machine hammered symmetric pattern organized rows full lathed both sides lathed drum kit. treated studio. Neumann U47, German V72 tube pre, German tube console, vari-mu, Pultec passive program EQ. tape 15ips plate reverb.",
